Here, `node` is the quantifier, and `body` is its body (a string). After `node_conv_to_str_node(node, body)`, `node` is overwritten with a copy of `body`'s content. Then `body` is freed. But `body` was the child of `node`. After `node` is overwritten, the link from `node` to `body` is lost. So freeing `body` is correct.

But what if `body` is also referenced from somewhere else? In a normal regex tree, each node has exactly one parent, so this shouldn't happen.

Let me look at the `divide_look_behind_alternatives` function:

```c
divide_look_behind_alternatives(Node* node)
{
  Node *head, *np, *insert_node;
  AnchorNode* an = ANCHOR_(node);
  int anc_type = an->type;

  head = NODE_ANCHOR_BODY(an);
  np = NODE_CAR(head);
  node_swap(node, head);
  NODE_CAR(node) = head;
  NODE_BODY(head) = np;

  np = node;
  while (IS_NOT_NULL(np = NODE_CDR(np))) {
    insert_node = onig_node_copy(head);
    CHECK_NULL_RETURN_MEMERR(insert_node);
    NODE_BODY(insert_node) = NODE_CAR(np);
    NODE_CAR(np) = insert_node;
  }
  // ...
}
```

This function modifies the tree structure significantly. It swaps nodes and creates copies. If `quantifiers_memory_node_info` is called on a tree that has been modified by `divide_look_behind_alternatives`, it might encounter nodes that are in an inconsistent state.

But the crash trace says `quantifiers_memory_node_info` -> `tune_quant` -> `tune_tree`. So the crash is during `tune_tree`, not after.

Let me look at the `tune_quant` function one more time. The `quantifiers_memory_node_info` is called on the body of a quantifier. If the body contains a `BAG_IF_ELSE` node, `quantifiers_memory_node_info` accesses `en->te.Then` and `en->te.Else`. If these pointers are stale (pointing to freed memory), that would cause a use-after-free.

But when would `en->te.Then` or `en->te.Else` point to freed memory? Only if the tree was modified after `quantifiers_memory_node_info` was called. But `quantifiers_memory_node_info` is called at the beginning of `tune_quant`, before `tune_tree(body, ...)` is called. So the tree shouldn't have been modified yet.

